# dist/ is build output, and right now it is COMMITTED build output — the exception this file used to
# forbid outright. The app fetches its catalogue from
# raw.githubusercontent.com/zeraix/registry/main/dist, an origin that can serve nothing which is not
# committed, so the publish workflow rebuilds both feeds and pushes them back on every merge
# (.github/workflows/publish.yml).
#
# The risk the old rule guarded against is real and unchanged: a feed edited by hand goes stale the
# moment a plugin lands, and a stale feed is a rollback waiting to be served. What makes this safe
# enough to live with is that nothing writes dist/ by hand — the builder derives each sequence from
# the published feed so it can only climb, rewrites nothing when the catalogue has not changed, and
# refuses to publish a digest taken from a modified working tree.
#
# When the publish endpoint exists, put /dist back here and let the endpoint serve the feeds.

# The app checkout the workflows borrow the validator from. Never part of this repository.
/.app/

# The app's built-in skills are ALSO not committed — but that rule lives in plugins/zeraix/.gitignore,
# which the exporter regenerates with one entry per generated skill. It is deliberately not a
# wildcard over the namespace: hand-authored official plugins (zeraix/office-suite) live beside the
# generated ones and must be committed, and a namespace-wide ignore silently swallowed them.
